  <h2 id="safetyTitle" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Safety guide</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-mute">Short, practical habits that protect you whether or not you use this tool.</p>
  <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
    <details class="card p-0"><summary class="flex min-h-[56px] items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-3"><i data-lucide="user-round-x" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-mint"></i><span class="font-semibold">Recognize impersonation</span></span><i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="chev h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-mute"></i></summary><p class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-mute">Scammers borrow the names of banks, police, courts, delivery firms, and tech support. A familiar name, logo, or caller ID proves nothing, because all of them can be copied. Judge the request, not the label.</p></details>
    <details class="card p-0"><summary class="flex min-h-[56px] items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-3"><i data-lucide="timer" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-warn"></i><span class="font-semibold">Why urgency and threats deserve scrutiny</span></span><i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="chev h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-mute"></i></summary><p class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-mute">Pressure such as “act within one hour” or “you will be arrested” is designed to stop you from thinking. Real organizations rarely demand instant payment or secrecy. Slow down and check on your own.</p></details>
    <details class="card p-0"><summary class="flex min-h-[56px] items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-3"><i data-lucide="banknote" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-danger"></i><span class="font-semibold">Spot suspicious payment requests</span></span><i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="chev h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-mute"></i></summary><p class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-mute">Be wary of gift cards, cryptocurrency, wire transfers to “safe accounts,” and fees you must pay to receive money or avoid a penalty. These methods are hard to reverse.</p></details>
    <details class="card p-0"><summary class="flex min-h-[56px] items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-3"><i data-lucide="link" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-sky2"></i><span class="font-semibold">Handle unexpected links</span></span><i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="chev h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-mute"></i></summary><p class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-mute">Don’t log in through a link you were sent. Open the official app or a bookmark you saved earlier. Shortened links and look-alike domains hide where you will really land.</p></details>
    <details class="card p-0"><summary class="flex min-h-[56px] items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-3"><i data-lucide="lock-keyhole" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-ultra"></i><span class="font-semibold">Never share authentication codes</span></span><i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="chev h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-mute"></i></summary><p class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-mute">A one-time code is the key to your account. No genuine support agent needs it from you. If someone asks for it, stop.</p></details>
    <details class="card p-0"><summary class="flex min-h-[56px] items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-3"><i data-lucide="phone-call" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-mint"></i><span class="font-semibold">Verify with contact details you find yourself</span></span><i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="chev h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-mute"></i></summary><p class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-mute">Look up the organization’s number or website from a card, statement, or official source you trust, not from the message. Then ask whether the request is real.</p></details>
    <details class="card p-0 md:col-span-2"><summary class="flex min-h-[56px] items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-3"><i data-lucide="life-buoy" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-danger"></i><span class="font-semibold">If you already shared money or credentials</span></span><i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="chev h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-mute"></i></summary><p class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-mute">Contact your bank or payment provider right away and ask what can be done. Change affected passwords through the official website, turn on multi-factor sign-in, and watch your accounts. Keep the messages as evidence and report the scam through your country’s official channels.</p></details>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-mute">ScamShield AI is not a replacement for professional cybersecurity advice, financial institutions, law enforcement, or official support channels.</p>
